        "sha": "ed36f7274524b75b44b7fb0dfa4ef1d9c657fe93",
        "message": "test: keep failed sequences and their nested groups literal (#169)\n\nBash keeps a group literal, along with every group nested in it, when its\nbody has a top-level `..` but is not a valid sequence. A `}` only closes a\ngroup once a top-level `,` or `..` has come before it, so a `{` with no\ncomma can run past its matching `}` to a later one and become such a\nfailed sequence. main already follows both rules, but no test pinned\nthem, so #166 could change them without a test failing."
