        "sha": "7257c14239476205b4b0bf7e47b07b3e7a517be6",
        "message": "chore: cover comparator normalization (#917)\n\n## Summary\n- Add regression fixtures and integration coverage for comparator\nwhitespace, equality boundaries, and malformed loose alternatives.\n- Cover long prerelease identifiers, build-metadata normalization, and\nexisting version limits across strict/loose and prerelease options.\n- Tests only; no production behavior changes.\n\n## Stack\nFirst of two stacked PRs; followed by #918. Contains only commit\n1eda6b48b211d87b9f5857a6e53361abe7622ef8. Merge this PR before the\nperformance implementation.\n\n## Validation\nFull `npm test` (including coverage, ESLint, and template checks) passes\non the combined stack.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 03b4a44c-26a3-4d56-9b26-cd46006844c6"
      },
      {
        "sha": "69b305d8a243c1ae9e0982dbe67217ab2bb9474b",
        "message": "fix: improve range parsing performance (#918)\n\n## Summary\n- Replace comparator whitespace normalization with a regex-free scanner\nthat preserves legacy match boundaries.\n- Cache numeric lookahead to avoid repeatedly scanning overlapping digit\nruns.\n- Share the ECMAScript whitespace definition between production and\ntests, using a byte lookup table rather than a Set.\n- Add legacy compatibility checks and large-prefix/numeric-input\nregression coverage.\n\n## Stack\nOriginally stacked on #917, which was squash-merged into `main` as\n7257c14239476205b4b0bf7e47b07b3e7a517be6. Rebased onto `main` after that\nmerge so this PR contains only the comparator normalization\nimplementation and its tests. The implementation patch is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n- Full `npm test` passed: 54 test files, 100% coverage, ESLint, and\ntemplate checks.\n- Differential review: 302,520 scanner cases and 100,000 Range cases\nmatched the parent implementation.\n- Whitespace lookup: 196,608 differential cases matched the original\nscanner across all UTF-16 code units.\n- Large invalid-prefix parsing improved dramatically; numeric-lookahead\naccess counts scaled linearly through one million characters.\n\n## Performance tradeoff\nLocal Node v26 benchmarks showed approximately 6–7% slower ordinary\nuncached Range parsing versus the original regex. The shared byte-table\nlookup did not introduce the additional slowdown observed with Set-based\nmembership checks. Measurements are local microbenchmarks, not\ncross-runtime guarantees.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCopilot-Session: 03b4a44c-26a3-4d56-9b26-cd46006844c6"
      },
      {
        "sha": "b37b033b585ad5e575afeccadb426ea41bc6cea4",
        "message": "chore: release 7.8.6 (#940)\n\n:robot: I have created a release *beep* *boop*\n---\n\n\n## [7.8.6](https://github.com/npm/node-semver/compare/v7.8.5...v7.8.6)\n(2026-11-02)\n### Bug Fixes\n*\n[`69b305d`](https://github.com/npm/node-semver/commit/69b305d8a243c1ae9e0982dbe67217ab2bb9474b)\n[#918](https://github.com/npm/node-semver/pull/918) improve range\nparsing performance (#918) (@reggi, @Copilot)\n### Chores\n*\n[`7257c14`](https://github.com/npm/node-semver/commit/7257c14239476205b4b0bf7e47b07b3e7a517be6)\n[#917](https://github.com/npm/node-semver/pull/917) cover comparator\nnormalization (#917) (@reggi, @Copilot)\n\n---\nThis PR was generated with [Release\nPlease](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please). See\n[documentation](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please#release-please).\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>"
